<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aulikara dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th–6th century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aulikara dynasty ruled the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandsaur">Dashapura</a>, modern Mandsaur in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a>, in the fifth and sixth centuries CE, at first as subordinates of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a>. Its most famous king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yasodharman">Yashodharman</a>, claimed victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huna-people">Huna</a> ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mihirakula">Mihirakula</a> around 528 and boasted in his Mandsaur pillar inscriptions of conquests across northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. After him the dynasty disappears from the record.</p></div>
<p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/state/aulikara-dynasty">State page: history, lineage and connections &rarr;</a></p>
